<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ ADRs mostly firmer as Dow climbs 44 points.</title>
<headline>NZ ADRs mostly firmer as Dow climbs 44 points.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand ADRs were mostly firmer in late afternoon New York trade, where by 7.40 a.m. NZT the Dow Industrials Index was up 44.73 points at 6,426.3.</p>
<p>Price movements of NZ stocks listed in the U.S., Britain and Australia.</p>
<p>Company	Exchange    Last	  Net change</p>
<p>FCL Bldg	 N.Y.    US$29 7/8	 +0 3/8 *</p>
<p>FCL Engy	 N.Y.    US$27 7/8	 +0 1/2 *</p>
<p>FCL Paper	N.Y.    US$19	     +0 1/4 *</p>
<p>FCL Forest     N.Y.    US$15 7/8	 +0 1/4 *</p>
<p>Telecom	  N.Y.    US$83 1/2	 +1 3/8 *</p>
<p>Tranz Rail     N.Y.    US$17 1/2	 -0 1/4 *</p>
<p>Evergreen	N.Y. (untraded. last trade 8 3/8)</p>
<p>Thistle	  London  173 p	     +3 1/2</p>
<p>Guinness Peat  London  32		  nil</p>
<p>Brierley	 London  54</p>
<p>NZ IT	    London  242		 +0 1/2</p>
<p>Foreign &amp; Col  London  150 3/4	   +0 1/4</p>
<p>Templeton	London  130		 +3</p>
<p>Lion	    Sydney  A$3.05	     -0.03</p>
<p>Goodman	 Sydney  A$1.60	     +0.03</p>
<p>Macraes	 Sydney  A$3.01	     nil</p>
<p>Notes - In New York, Telecom's American Depository Receipts are traded in bundles of 16 shares, while both the Fletcher Challenge shares are in bundles of 10 each. Tranz Rail ADSs are groups of three ordinary shares. Evergreen ADRs are traded in bundles of 20.</p>
<p>- London prices are mid-rates.</p>
<p>- Asterisk * means stock is still trading</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
